    "task_id": "explicit-phase-entry-s1-contract",
    "goal": "Implement Slice S1 of Initiative explicit-phase-entry per docs/specs/explicit-phase-entry.spec.md (T4): every packaged contract copy makes the Planner and Brainstorm stop after candidate validation without invoking Enrollment, and makes native Enrollment the first step of an explicit imm-run entry. User scenarios SCN-1 and SCN-2 belong to this Slice.",
    "acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "EPE-S1-A1",
        "assertion": "Per T4 and decision D1 of docs/specs/explicit-phase-entry.spec.md (source: user decisions U2, U3): in dist/imm-planner.md, skills/imm-planner/SKILL.md, dist/imm-brainstorm.md and all three BASELINE.md copies, no route invokes the native Enrollment gate from the Planner or Brainstorm; the Planner Next Action reports the validated candidate and names a literal-user imm-run entry as the only next step; the phrases 'without a second human stop' as a Planner route and 'execution-bearing requests open the native gate directly' are absent from every copy, while the Plan-only stop wording remains. Seam: new tests/explicit-phase-entry-planner-contract.test.ts reading those files; it must contain at least one test and fail when any copy keeps the removed route.",
        "verification": "{\n  \"contract\": \"assurance_kernel/verification_descriptor/v2\",\n  \"command\": {\n    \"executable\": \"bun\",\n    \"argv\": [\n      \"test\",\n      \"tests/explicit-phase-entry-planner-contract.test.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"cwd\": \".\",\n    \"timeout_ms\": 180000,\n    \"max_output_bytes\": 131072\n  },\n  \"environment\": {\n    \"prepare\": null,\n    \"writable_paths\": []\n  }\n}\n"
